src/vendor/mir/ is the files listed in tools/mir-files.txt, copied from the
fork at the fork commit above. That commit is the upstream commit plus
exactly the patches listed, one commit each (design D12): the fork's master
mirrors upstream, its zumir branch carries the series on the upstream pin,
and each patch also sits alone on a fix/ branch cut from master, to become
an upstream pull request. tools/vendor.sh copies the tree; tools/verify-vendor
re-derives it and fails on any other difference (vendor.yaml runs it).
tools/mir-abi.txt holds the enums and structs of the vendored mir.h, the
part a consumer of the C API compiles in (design D21).

A commit, not a release, is pinned on purpose (design D2): the only tag
misses two and a half years of fixes. Every bump re-runs the spike's checks.

The patches, with the fork branch that carries each one alone:

  ea7f1643  item_name_ptr() returns after mir_assert (FALSE); three hash
            probes initialise every reg_desc_t field. Rtools gcc 14
            -Wreturn-type and -Wuninitialized. fix/rtools-gcc-warnings;
            upstream: not filed yet (#30).
  773a4834  VirtualFree (addr, 0, MEM_RELEASE). fix/windows-virtualfree;
            upstream issue https://github.com/vnmakarov/mir/issues/496.
  dafb8e1b  An unused variable in mir-gen.c; two set-but-unused ones on Apple
            aarch64. clang -Wall on macOS. fix/unused-variables; upstream:
            not filed yet (#30).
  f35a0021  No `;` after the DEF_* macro invocations at file scope (97
            lines). gcc -pedantic. fix/no-extra-semicolons; upstream: not
            filed yet (#30).
  6edb5ce2  mem_page_size (void), the only empty parameter list. clang
            -pedantic -Wstrict-prototypes. fix/strict-prototypes; upstream:
            not filed yet (#30).
  1571f134  snprintf with the destination array's size for all ten sprintf
            calls. R's compiled-code check rejects sprintf.
            fix/snprintf; upstream: not filed yet (#30).
  0b8063f7  MIR_finish clears curr_func and curr_module first, so a context
            whose MIR_finish_func was left by a longjmp can be finished
            (the spike's patch 0001). fix/finish-clears-current; upstream:
            not filed yet (#30).
  4c27a18f  MIR_init2's version check and _MIR_init's first allocation
            return NULL instead of exiting: both run before an error
            function can be installed. fix/init-returns-null; upstream:
            not filed yet (#30).

Not patched, built differently instead (design §4.2):

  - exit, abort and writes to stderr are redirected to zumir by macros in
    src/zumir_mir_stdio.h, defined in the wrapper files just before MIR's
    sources; MIR's code is unchanged for it.
  - MIR's sources are compiled with gcc's -fno-tree-sra
    (src/zumir_mir_gcc.h), as upstream's makefile does: without it Rtools
    gcc miscompiles the interpreter.
  - The interpreter is compiled with MIR_DIRECT_DISPATCH (src/zumir_mir.c),
    a switch instead of computed `goto *`, which -pedantic reports.
  - No -fsigned-char: MIR's own tests pass with -funsigned-char on x86-64
    (2026-11-13) and on Linux aarch64, where char is unsigned, in
    tools/ci/platform.sh, so the core does not depend on it.
  - Symbols are hidden by $(C_VISIBILITY) and src/zumir-win.def; MIR's
    sources are unchanged for it.
  - On a CPU MIR does not target, and on Windows aarch64 (D25), the wrapper
    files compile nothing (src/zumir_mir.h).

Not vendored: c2mir (Stage 8), the tests, benchmarks, llvm2mir, mir2c, the
drivers and utilities. The README's Mozilla Public License mention is about
NanoJIT, not any MIR file.
